 The files to change are the ones the findings' `location` keys name, or the gate findings name.
 A `fix` key that opens with `site not found —` marks a finding whose `location` names only where the defect shows:
 find the site the change belongs at before you edit.
+A `fix` key that names a fact as unverified rests on that fact:
+read it in the code before you apply the change, and give the finding its disposition below with what you read.
 Weigh each finding twice: its premise, and the change its `fix` key proposes.
 Give it exactly one of three dispositions, decided in this order.
 
diff --git a/contracts/stencils/loom/loom-block-plan-cards.md b/contracts/stencils/loom/loom-block-plan-cards.md
index 7c507f3b0..b2e1d9cec 100644
--- a/contracts/stencils/loom/loom-block-plan-cards.md
+++ b/contracts/stencils/loom/loom-block-plan-cards.md
@@ -53,6 +53,12 @@ A test that calls only the refusal's error constructor does not reach it.
 A card whose `**Intent:**` covers every instance of one kind across the repository lists every file holding one.
 Its Intent names the repository search that found them, so a reviewer can re-run it to prove the list complete.
 
+Each claim a card makes about the code is one you read in the code:
+who reads or writes a field or value, through every function on the call chain;
+whether a member is exported or otherwise visible from the package that uses it, and whether a test or seam can reach it from there;
+and which input reaches a branch once every check before it passes.
+No card's rule or claim contradicts another card's, or is made false by another card's change.
+
 A field with no content is omitted entirely — never write a `none` sentinel on any field.
 
 **`Uses:` names what the card reads but does not change — never a target.**
diff --git a/contracts/stencils/loom/loom-rubric-plan-review.md b/contracts/stencils/loom/loom-rubric-plan-review.md
index ca33eaa75..e5e914d3e 100644
--- a/contracts/stencils/loom/loom-rubric-plan-review.md
+++ b/contracts/stencils/loom/loom-rubric-plan-review.md
@@ -55,6 +55,15 @@ Do not flag any of the following as a finding:
   One card per independently reviewable unit, not one card per literal symbol.
   A private supporting type, or a constructor inseparable from its type, belongs in the other symbol's card;
   a symbol that is part of a module's public surface, or reused across packages, gets its own card even when one card is its only consumer, and a helper serving one surface is bundled into that surface's card.
+- **Card claims against the code.**
+  Each claim a card makes about the code is read in the code it names:
+  who reads or writes a field or value, through every function on the call chain;
+  whether a member is exported or otherwise visible from the package that uses it, and whether a test or seam can reach it from there;
+  and which input reaches a branch once every check before it passes.
+  A claim the code disproves is a finding that names the code disproving it.
+- **Cards against each other.**
+  Each card is read against every other card.
+  A card whose rule contradicts another card's, or whose claim another card's change makes false, is a finding that names both cards.
 - **A repository-wide intent.**
   A card whose `**Intent:**` covers every instance of one kind across the repository needs a search that proves its targets complete.
   It is a finding when its Intent names no repository search that found its targets.
